	abstract = {The onset of a microseismic signal on a geophone trace is determined by modeling the noise and seismic signal in windows using the Akaike Information Criterion (AIC). Initially developed to predict an optimal order for an autorecursive filter, the criterion can be used to demark the point of two adjacent time series with different underlying statistics. The AIC first‐break pick algorithm is robust in the presence of high‐amplitude random noise, computationally fast and could be implemented automatically.},
